## General Principles

- Write functional components with hooks (no class components)
- Keep components small, focused, and reusable (< 200 lines)
- Use TypeScript for type safety and better IDE support
- Follow React best practices and latest patterns
- Prioritize composition over inheritance
- Write self-documenting code with clear intent
- Use meaningful component and variable names
- Optimize performance with appropriate React hooks
- Handle errors gracefully with error boundaries
- Write accessible components following WCAG guidelines

